  },
  "name": "Extract invoice data from Gmail attachments to Google Sheets (Advanced)",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "87e8caf5-e857-4120-913e-e6e0f9355584",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -224,
        -128
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#D0CD67",
        "width": 1144,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "### How it works (Advanced version)\nThis workflow watches your Gmail inbox for incoming invoices, reads PDF attachments, and uses AI to extract structured invoice data before saving it to Google Sheets — with dedup, validation, error logging, and approval alerts built in.\n\nFlow:\n1. Poll Gmail daily for emails with \"invoice\", \"bill\", or \"receipt\" + attachment.\n2. Split multi-attachment emails into individual items.\n3. Skip attachments already processed in a previous run (workflow static data, keyed on message id + file name).\n4. Route by file type: PDFs go through text extraction; anything else (images, docs, etc.) is logged to a \"ManualReview\" sheet tab instead of silently failing.\n5. AI Agent (GPT-4.1-mini, unchanged) extracts structured invoice JSON from the PDF text.\n6. A Code node normalizes the JSON and validates it: flags missing fields and checks that subtotal − discount + tax = grand total.\n7. If the AI response failed to parse or is missing critical fields, the row is logged to an \"Errors\" sheet tab instead of the main tracker.\n8. If the invoice is high-value (over the threshold, default PKR 100,000) or has a validation mismatch, you get an email alert before it's logged — otherwise it's appended straight to the tracker.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect Gmail (OAuth2, with Send permission — needed for the approval alert email) in the Gmail Trigger and Send Approval Alert nodes.\n2. Connect OpenAI in the OpenAI Chat Model node (GPT-4.1-mini or similar).\n3. In your Google Sheet, create THREE tabs: your existing invoice tracker tab, plus new \"Errors\" and \"ManualReview\" tabs. Re-select the correct tab in the \"Log Errors\" and \"Log Manual Review\" nodes after creating them (the sheet reference won't auto-resolve on import).\n4. Adjust the high-value threshold (100000) inside the \"Needs Review?\" node to match your business.\n5. Adjust the Gmail search filter if you want to widen/narrow which emails get scanned.\n6. Activate the workflow.\n\n### Notes\n- Dedup uses n8n's workflow static data, so it persists across polls as long as the workflow stays saved/active — it resets if you clear static data or move the workflow.\n- Non-PDF attachments (images, Word docs, etc.) are NOT auto-extracted in this version — they're routed to ManualReview so nothing is silently dropped. Adding OCR/vision support for those is a natural next upgrade.\n- Model is intentionally left as GPT-4.1-mini; swap it in the OpenAI Chat Model node if you want to try Claude or Gemini."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
